---
description: Karzar Cursor economy policy — cheap-first model routing and bounded exploration
alwaysApply: true
---

Optimize for accepted PRs per unit of model usage.

Default:
- Use Cursor/cheap model for repo mapping, targeted search, docs, mechanical edits, test scaffolding, CI triage, and evidence formatting.
- Escalate to frontier reasoning only for payment/auth/security boundaries, concurrency/transactions, architecture ambiguity, or final P0/P1 review.
- After a frontier decision is made, return mechanical implementation/cleanup to a cheaper model when safe.
- Avoid repeated full-repo scans, repeated summaries, and re-reading already-resolved context.
- Prefer concise outputs and exact paths/tests over narrative.
- Do not use Fast/Cloud/parallel agents by default; use only when the task benefit clearly justifies extra spend.
